<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Tailgate</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="top">
      <a class="brand" href="/">Tailgate</a>
      <nav>
        <%= link_to "Feed", feed_path %>
        <%= link_to "Members", members_path %>
        <%= link_to "Fan-out inspector", inspector_path %>
      </nav>
      <%= form_with url: viewer_path, method: :post, class: "viewer" do |f| %>
        <label>Browsing as</label>
        <%= f.select :handle, Member.order(:handle).pluck(:handle), { selected: viewer&.handle }, onchange: "this.form.requestSubmit()" %>
      <% end %>
    </header>
    <main>
      <% if notice %><p class="flash"><%= notice %></p><% end %>
      <%= yield %>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <p>Tailgate is a social activity layer for a picks app: Rails owns members, the follow graph and activities; <code>fanoutd</code> (Go) owns timeline fan-out. Exactly-once delivery per (follower, activity) is a unique index, not a promise.</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
